				113
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Enforce consistent vertical spacing, harden shell/encryption paths\n\nApply blank-line-after-declaration formatting uniformly across ~260 Rust source files, removing discretionary spacing variations that accumulated during iterative development. The change is purely cosmetic in the large majority of files — no logic, control flow, or semantics are altered.\n\nThree functional changes are bundled in this pass:\n\n- Key.rs: `DeriveKey` now returns `Result<[u8; 32], String>` and `ReadMachineId` returns `Option<String>`, removing the fallback to executable-path hash when no hardware-bound machine ID is available. This eliminates a path where ciphertext could be encrypted with a predictable seed on headless or restricted systems. Callers in Encrypt.rs/Decrypt.rs propagate the `Err` upward.\n- InstallShellCommand.rs, MoveItemToTrash.rs, UninstallShellCommand.rs: Replace string-interpolated AppleScript/PowerShell arguments with environment-variable-passed paths using `quoted form of` / `$env:` patterns, preventing shell injection via crafted file paths.\n- Info.plist: Switch `TierSchemeAssets` from `Embedded` to `FileSystem`, selecting the disk-layout asset deployment mode at the daemon config level rather than relying solely on build-time env vars.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "4dcdc190d8f11e7fb102b0b16c38872367979fbf"
		}
	],
